            <ArticleTitle>Parasystolic ventricular tachycardia with variable exit block.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>411-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This case is an example of ventricular parasystolic tachycardia associated with variable expressions of ectopic-ventricular (E-V) exit block. The exit block manifested with 2:1, 3:2, 4:3 and higher ratios of E-V conductions, interspaced with periods of 1:1 conduction. Concealed E-V conduction of the ectopic impulse could also be deduced.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
